<div id="menu"></div>

<main class="page">
    <h1>Buttons</h1>
    <p class="lead">UIButton is any clickable element. Actions bind by selector when the controller is presented.</p>

    <section class="demo">
        <h2>@IBAction</h2>
        <p>One method per button, bound by selector. <kbd>↑</kbd> and <kbd>↓</kbd> are bound the same way with <code>Keyboard.arrowUp</code> and <code>Keyboard.arrowDown</code>.</p>
        <div class="row">
            <button id="buttons-decrement" class="button button-secondary">−</button>
            <span id="buttons-count" class="buttons-count">0</span>
            <button id="buttons-increment" class="button">+</button>
            <button id="buttons-reset" class="button button-secondary">Reset</button>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="demo">
        <h2>sendActions</h2>
        <p>Triggers another button's action from code, the way <code>sendActions(for:)</code> does.</p>
        <button id="buttons-remote" class="button button-secondary">Increment from code</button>
    </section>

    <section class="demo">
        <h2>addTarget and isEnabled</h2>
        <p>A UISwitch is a checkbox. Its <code>valueChanged</code> event is wired with <code>addTarget</code>, whose action receives <code>(target, sender)</code>, and it enables or disables the button.</p>
        <div class="row">
            <label class="switch"><input id="buttons-enabled-switch" type="checkbox" checked> Enabled</label>
            <button id="buttons-target" class="button">Tap me</button>
            <span id="buttons-target-output" class="buttons-output"></span>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
